00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:21,000
The Epic Fall of the American Indian

2
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Bury My Heart at Wounded Knee is a western, drama,
history film directed by Yves Simoneau.

3
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Beginning just after the bloody Sioux victory over General Custer at Little Big Horn, the story is told through two unique perspectives: Charles Eastman, a young, white-educated Sioux doctor
held up as living proof of the alleged success of assimilation, and Sitting Bull the proud Lakota chief whose tribe won the American Indians’ last major victory at Little Big Horn.

